<title>UK: SOCCER-MANCHESTER UNITED 0 BORUSSIA DORTMUND 1 - RESULT.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-MANCHESTER UNITED 0 BORUSSIA DORTMUND 1 - RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>MANCHESTER, England 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Borussia Dortmund</p>
<p>of Germany beat Manchester United of England 1-0 in the second</p>
<p>leg of their European Cup semifinal at Old Trafford on Wednesday</p>
<p>to win the tie 2-0 on aggregate.</p>
<p>Goal: Borussia Dortmund: Lars Ricken 8</p>
<p>Halftime:  0-1</p>
<p>Attendance: 53,500</p>
<p>Manchester United: 1-Peter Schmeichel; 2-Gary Neville, 6-Gary</p>
<p>Pallister, 4-David May (12-Paul Scholes 87), 28-Phil Neville,</p>
<p>5-Ronny Johnsen, 8- Nicky Butt, 10-David Beckham, 7-Eric</p>
<p>Cantona, 9-Andy Cole, 20- Ole Solskjaer (11-Ryan Giggs 57)</p>
<p>Borussia Dortmund: 1-Stefan Klos; 15-Juergen Kohler, 20-</p>
<p>Wolfgang Feiersinger, 16-Martin Kree, 14-Paul Lambert, 7-Stefan</p>
<p>Reuter (23-Rene Tretschok 24), 10-Andreas Moeller, 18-Lars</p>
<p>Ricken (8-Michael Zorc 61), 17-Joerg Heinrich, 13-Karlheinz</p>
<p>Reidle (11-Heiko Herrlich 72), 9-Stephane Chapuisat.</p>
<p>Referee: Urs Meier, Switzerland</p>
</text>
